  "narrative": {
    "text": "Figure 8.4(b), the limit supermatrix W∞ for the same ANP model, in the same SuperDecisions window. The structural fact to read off it: **every column is identical**, each holding C1 0.079748, C2 0.199064, C3 0.292616, A1 0.240932, A2 0.187639, with Goal_Node 0.000000. That is what convergence of a column-stochastic supermatrix to its limit means — the long-run priority no longer depends on where the walk started — and it is why ANP reads its answer off any single column. A \"Done\" button is at the foot of the window.",
